 - Prefer complete sentences over fragments using semicolons
 
+## Headings in mail
+
+When a message is long enough to need sections, head each one with
+an org-style heading: one or more "*" at the left margin, a space,
+and the title. Use "**" for a subsection. Pat's notmuch folds each
+such section under its heading, so he can skim a long message and
+open only the parts he needs. Titles underlined with dashes do not
+fold. For the same reason, start list items with "-", never with
+"*" at the margin, which would read as a heading. A short reply
+needs no headings.
+
